       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. The order is double the maximum.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and they give no added glycemic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n1. **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what \"1700\" was meant to be.\n2. **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n3. **Another dose or formulation**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg, or extended-release.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose is intentional. Otherwise, tell me which option to enter."
      }
